#: 0e667f48e00045e78dc25619d12805c9
msgid "Connect your autopilot to your computer with the usb cable"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compass-setup-advanced.rst:122
#: 0cfa7dbc98d7406fae1842dc271257e8
msgid "Open the **Initial Setup \\| Optional Hardware \\| Compass/Motor Calib** screen"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compass-setup-advanced.rst:123
#: ef83ac4f5c354765839b54f629883cfd
msgid "Press the **Start** button"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compass-setup-advanced.rst:128
#: 5c35543ef8b5437e941c6e102a17d7e3
msgid "You should hear your ESCs arming beep"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compass-setup-advanced.rst:129
#: 8be7e2c15fe94c78a9365717bcc40357
msgid "Raise the throttle slowly to between 50% ~ 75% (the props will spin!) for 5 ~ 10 seconds"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compass-setup-advanced.rst:131
#: 98c544949e3c497aaedab47d32ead5e5
msgid "Quickly bring the throttle back down to zero"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compass-setup-advanced.rst:132
#: 52502309955c4384ba787f231f13b8c5
msgid "Press the **Finish** button to complete the calibration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compass-setup-advanced.rst:133
#: 69ca1e4b284e488480f4258bfe7438b9
msgid "Check the % of interference displayed.  If it is less than 30% then your compass interference is acceptable and you should see good Loiter, RTL and AUTO performance.  If it is 31% ~ 60% then the interference is in the \"grey zone\" where it may be ok (some users are fine, some are not).  If it is higher than 60% you should try moving your autopilot further up and away from the sources of interference or consider purchasing an external compass (or :ref:`GPS+compass module<common-positioning-landing-page>` (some of these))."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compass-setup-advanced.rst:148
#: 6df41b8561ff46e2b20eaaaaf9073572
msgid "Automatic Offset Calibration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compass-setup-advanced.rst:150
#: d5ac095bf3454528bab29f5f6dbafb7a
msgid "DO NOT USE THIS WITH GPS-DERIVED YAW! ie :ref:`common-gps-for-yaw` in  firmware versions before 4.5.2!"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compass-setup-advanced.rst:152
#: 89f3cb64a6a64899916bb6fb6eed6b39
msgid "In the 4.0 and later releases of ArduPilot, an automatic offset learning feature is available. The :ref:`COMPASS_LEARN<COMPASS_LEARN>` parameter determines how this feature works. This is for advanced users and not recommended."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compass-setup-advanced.rst:154
#: 14453ea8fc25481abf194c8c45431ea6
msgid "If set to 3, the offsets will be learned automatically during flight, be saved, and this parameter reset to 0. Position control modes (Loiter, Auto, etc.) should not be used while the offsets are being learned."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compass-setup-advanced.rst:156
#: 571437160eb5440c9f1b4b6bc539d4b1
msgid "Setting :ref:`COMPASS_LEARN<COMPASS_LEARN>` to 1 or 2 is not recommended. These modes are deprecated and are either non-functional, or still in development."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compass-setup-advanced.rst:158
#: f6ea294c42404ab39e597da62b478b4b
msgid "The procedure for :ref:`COMPASS_LEARN<COMPASS_LEARN>` = 3 is:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compass-setup-advanced.rst:160
#: a8a099acd0884fa49464e2a32fe3c372
msgid "set :ref:`COMPASS_LEARN<COMPASS_LEARN>` = 3. The message “CompassLearn: Initialised” will appear on the MP’s message tab (it does not appear in red letters on the HUD)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compass-setup-advanced.rst:161
#: 22765c947d0642f8a31573bab232b10f
msgid "“Bad Compass” will appear but this is nothing to be worried about. We will hopefully make this disappear before the final release."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compass-setup-advanced.rst:162
#: 95ca89e4705e4d60b2c54f9320691af3
msgid "Arm and drive/fly the vehicle around in whatever mode you like, do some turns “CompassLearn: have earth field” should appear on MP’s message tab and then eventually “CompassLearn: finished”."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compass-setup-advanced.rst:164
#: 390dd057895a4796a7ab98020903bad1
msgid "You MUST have a GPS lock and signal for this to be successful. Be sure the GPS has a clear \"view\" of the sky and there are no obstructions blocking the GPS signals."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compass-setup-advanced.rst:166
#: c5136cf1f3f8429c9505c6d0b1a0b2b4
msgid "If you want you can check the :ref:`COMPASS_LEARN<COMPASS_LEARN>` parameter has been set back to zero (you may need to refresh parameters to see this) and the COMPASS_OFS_X/Y/Z values will have changed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compass-setup-advanced.rst:167
#: e039d0929ad9486b96029be653190173
msgid "This method can also be evoked using the RCxOPTION for \"Compass Learn\". It will activate when the channel goes above 1800uS and automatically complete and save."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compass-setup-advanced.rst:172
#: 511d54af42454e4eabcaece3dc4aa6a3
msgid "Compass error messages"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compass-setup-advanced.rst:174
#: 843e723ce7434ab79ada5a2159b15194
msgid "**Compass Health**: The compass has not sent a signal for at least half a second."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compass-setup-advanced.rst:176
#: 02b313471966419fb3827692d25863fd
msgid "**Compass Variance**: In the EKF solution, compass heading disagrees with the heading estimate from other inertial sensors. Clicking the EKF button on the Mission Planner HUD will show the magnitude of the error."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compass-setup-advanced.rst:180
#: 36fe7631126c4757a66c570a37b5532d
msgid "**Compass Not Calibrated**: The compass needs to be calibrated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compass-setup-advanced.rst:181
#: 9856aed549174ae09e640e059560e6ec
msgid "**Compass Offsets High**: One of your compass offsets exceeds 600, indicating likely magnetic interference. Check for sources of interference and try calibrating again."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compass-setup-advanced.rst:186
#: f83a6c19561844ee9b559a06953c8d45
msgid "Refining Calibration Parameters using a Flight Log"
msgstr ""

